    {
      "id": "policy-paraphrase",
      "question": "Can I switch dorms?",
      "httpStatus": 200,
      "response": {
        "answer": "Yes\u2014Ramapo has a Room Change Process, so switching dorms/rooms is possible through Residence Life, but requests are not guaranteed because they depend on suitable space availability. The process is not first-come, first-served, and if requests conflict, priority may be based on highest earned credits. [Residence Life](https://www.ramapo.edu/reslife/rcp/)\n\nIf your room change is approved, you must check in to the new housing assignment. If you do not complete an approved room change, a $75 improper checkout fee is charged. Once a room change is approved, cancellations cannot occur because other residents\u2019 approved assignments may be affected. [Residence Life](https://www.ramapo.edu/reslife/rcp/)\n\nResidence Life publishes an online Room Change Request Form as the way to access the process. [Residence Life](https://www.ramapo.edu/reslife/rcp/)\n\nIf you switch into The Village or The College Park Apartments during the open room change period, you may be able to drop your meal plan by emailing mealplan@ramapo.edu by the semester\u2019s meal plan change deadline. If no meal plan is selected, Ramapo says the Tasty 10 meal plan will be assigned automatically. Students who move there after the meal-plan drop deadline cannot remove an existing meal plan. [Residence Life](https://www.ramapo.edu/reslife/rcp/)\n\nIf you want, I can also help you find the Room Change Request page or the best housing contact to ask about your specific situation.",
